.TH TINYKV 1 "2026-11-19" "tinykv 1.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tinykv \- command line tool for the tinykv embedded key-value store
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tinykv
.I command database
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tinykv
operates on tinykv databases: single append-only log files with
CRC-32 checksummed records and an in-memory hash index. One process may
hold a database read-write at a time; any number of read-only handles
are allowed.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI put " database key value"
Store a value. Keys and values are NUL-free shell strings; for binary
payloads use the library API.
.TP
.BI get " database key"
Print the value with a trailing newline.
.B \-\-raw
omits the newline;
.BI \-\-into= file
writes the exact stored bytes to a new file instead.
.TP
.BI exists " database key"
Print
.B exists
and exit 0 when the key is present; exit 2 when it is not.
.TP
.BI del " database key"
Delete a key. Absent keys exit 2 without writing anything.
.TP
.BI list " database"
Print
.B key<TAB>value
for every live key in sorted order. An optional
.I prefix
argument filters the output.
.TP
.BI keys " database"
Print one live key per line, optionally filtered by a prefix.
.TP
.BI count " database"
Print the number of live keys, optionally filtered by a prefix.
.TP
.BI stats " database"
Print storage statistics. With
.B \-\-json
the same numbers print as a JSON object including the version.
.TP
.BI compact " database"
Rewrite the log keeping only live records, atomically.
.TP
.BI verify " database"
Classify the log: exit 0 clean, 3 torn tail, 4 corruption. With
.B \-\-json
the status and last verified offset print as JSON.
.TP
.BI repair " database"
Show a repair plan (dry run). Add
.B \-\-yes
to apply: the original is preserved as
.IB database .bak,
a verified replacement is written to
.IB database .repair,
then swapped in atomically.
.B \-\-max-key= N
and
.B \-\-max-value= N
match databases opened with custom limits.
.TP
.BI copy " database new-database"
Consistent snapshot into a brand-new file.
.TP
.BI batch " database"
Import
.B key<TAB>value
lines from standard input;
.B \-\-sync= none|close|every
chooses the durability policy.
.TP
.BI import " database file"
Load the same line format from a file.
.TP
.BI export " database file"
Dump every live key/value as
.B key<TAB>value
lines into a new file.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Usage error or invalid input.
.TP
.B 2
Key not found.
.TP
.B 3
Torn tail detected.
.TP
.B 4
Corruption detected.
.TP
.B 5
Database locked by another process.
.TP
.B 6
Filesystem or output failure.
.SH FILES
Database files are created 0600. Repair leaves
.IB database .bak
next to the repaired database.
.SH SEE ALSO
The project README and docs/ directory: api.md, design.md,
durability.md, record-format.md, repair-mode-safety.md.
.SH AUTHOR
tinykv contributors
